    "result": "Excellent! The implementation is complete. Let me create a quick summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval` that allows failing CI jobs based on metric thresholds. Here's what was added:\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n\n**`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`**\n- Enhanced `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` object (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`)\n- Added threshold validation logic: metric passes if `score >= min`; fails if `score === null`\n- Report includes `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array with per-metric details\n\n**`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`**\n- Markdown reports now include a \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL for each threshold\n\n**`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`**\n- Added 5 comprehensive tests for threshold functionality\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli)\n\n**`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`**\n- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (can be given multiple times)\n- Validation function checks:\n  - Format: must be `<metric>=<number>`\n  - Value range: must be between 0 and 1\n  - Known metric: exact_match, toxicity, length_variance\n- Exit codes:\n  - **0** if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds given)\n  - **1** if any threshold fails\n  - **2** if threshold format/value is invalid or metric unknown\n\n### Documentation\n\n- Updated CLI README with complete `--threshold` option documentation\n- Added SDK code example showing threshold usage\n- Updated eval harness design document with threshold validation details\n\n### Key Features\n\n\u2705 Backward compatible - no changes when `--threshold` not used  \n\u2705 Supports custom metrics for SDK users  \n\u2705 Clear error messages listing valid metric IDs  \n\u2705 Reports always written regardless of pass/fail  \n\u2705 Works for SDK and CLI users\n\nThe feature is ready for use in CI/CD pipelines to gate deployments on model evaluation metrics.",
